<title>USA: Duke shuts 846 MW Oconee 3 nuclear unit.</title>
<headline>Duke shuts 846 MW Oconee 3 nuclear unit.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Duke Power Co's 846 megawatt (MW) Oconee 3 nuclear unit was shut late Thursday, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said Friday in its daily plant status report.</p>
<p>The unit, in Seneca, S.C., was expected to restart sometime today, the NRC reported.</p>
<p>Early Thursday the unit had been operating at 73 percent power and was undergoing startup testing following its maintenance outage which began last October.</p>
<p>The adjacent units 1 and 2, each rated at 846 MW, were both operating at full power.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +212-859-1628))</p>
